pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"charset","label":"Character encoding declared","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"lang","label":"Document language (lang) set","pass":true,"detail":"en"},{"id":"viewport","label":"Responsive viewport (zoom not disabled)","pass":true,"detail":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},{"id":"open-graph","label":"Open Graph tags (5/6)","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"twitter-card","label":"Twitter card metadata","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"open-social","label":"Open social presence (Mastodon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Center for Embedded Systems (CES)","description":"The last update is from 2023.The Center for Embedded Systems (CES) researches the technologies that enable sensing, communications, and computing in everyday things. Its purpose is to advance the field of embedded systems (hardware, software, and architectures), share advancements, and commercialize applications.CES conducts fundamental research that leads to improvements in personalized health care technologies, consumer electronics, aerospace and avionics, industrial automation, automotive and transportation, and security. CES connects industry with leading faculty members and student researchers on industry-led projects involving embedded systems in algorithms, applications, and architectures to develop products to meet market needs.An embedded system is an application-specific computing system found inside products such as home appliances, mobile handheld personal systems (e.g., cellphones, health monitors, assistive devices, cameras, electronic games), instrumentation, automobiles, aircraft, missiles, satellites, and nuclear power plants. Embedded systems are distinguished from general-purpose computing systems by their well-defined functionalities and stringent design constraints. Embedded systems encompass all of the four fundamental operational capabilities required to interface with the world at large - sensing, computing, control, and communication - which can now be integrated with single-chip multiprocessors. The ability to combine operational capabilities in this way has opened up new possibilities for application-specific computing.","url":"/centers/center-for-embedded-systems/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-embedded-systems/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-embedded-systems/","why":"A web app manifest is required for installability and controls how the app appears when launched."},{"id":"pwa-service-worker","label":"Service worker registered","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-embedded-systems/","why":"A service worker is what makes offline access, caching, and background sync possible."},{"id":"pwa-theme-color","label":"Theme color declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-embedded-systems/","why":"Theme color controls the browser chrome/status-bar color when the site is installed or bookmarked."},{"id":"pwa-apple-touch-icon","label":"Apple touch icon (iOS/bookmark icon)","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-embedded-systems/","why":"iOS uses this icon for home-screen bookmarks and \"Add to Home Screen\" — without it the icon falls back to a screenshot."},{"id":"manifest-parsed","label":"Manifest fetched and parsed successfully","status":"n/a","evidence":"No manifest declared","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-embedded-systems/","why":"A manifest that fails to parse cannot drive installability